\caption(The original dense disk workload yields near-rim flags and no flagged points inside the chosen radius-seven core on this sample. This observation does not erase the interior counterexample or establish a sampling-independent boundary guarantee.)
\alttext(A native circular disk of grey samples has red flagged samples near its outer rim. A thin circle shows the generator's radius-ten boundary at equal horizontal and vertical scales.)

> Radius and threshold are part of the result

For fixed points and threshold, increasing r adds directions. Splitting circular
gaps cannot enlarge the largest empty gap, so flags can disappear as the radius
grows. For fixed r, raising β also cannot add a flag. These monotonic statements
describe the rule; choosing parameters that match an unknown physical boundary
still needs information about sampling density, holes and the shape's scale.

The next program regenerates the same cloud, measures radius sensitivity at
0.55π, then changes the angular threshold at r=2.5. It reports the chosen core
separately. An absent flagged minimum is printed as none, using an explicit
has_flagged state rather than a large numerical sentinel.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cone_sensitivity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto p=dm::geometry::sample_disk_candidates(2500,10,1);
  const double original_threshold=.55*std::acos(-1.);
  std::vector<double> radii,flagged,inner_flagged;
  std::print("| radius at 0.55 pi | total flagged | chosen core flagged | pair visits | angle evaluations |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(double radius:{.25,.5,1.,2.5,5.}) {
    const auto a=dm::geometry::cone_surface_analyze(p,radius,original_threshold);
    const auto s=dm::geometry::radial_flag_summary(p,a.surface,7,9.4);
    radii.push_back(radius);flagged.push_back(s.flagged_points);inner_flagged.push_back(s.inner_flagged);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",radius,s.flagged_points,s.inner_flagged,a.work.pair_visits,a.work.angle_evaluations);
  }
  std::print("\n| threshold / pi at radius 2.5 | total flagged | chosen core flagged | minimum flagged radius |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(long double ratio:{.05L,.25L,.55L,1.L,2.L}) {
    const auto a=dm::geometry::cone_surface_analyze(p,2.5,ratio*std::acos(-1.L));
    const auto s=dm::geometry::radial_flag_summary(p,a.surface,7,9.4);
    std::print("| {:.2f} | {} | {} | {} |\n",ratio,s.flagged_points,s.inner_flagged,s.has_flagged?std::format("{:.6f}",s.min_flagged_radius):"none");
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(radii,flagged,"all flagged",{220,38,38},2).points(radii,flagged,"",{220,38,38},5)
      .line(radii,inner_flagged,"core flagged",{37,99,235},2).points(radii,inner_flagged,"",{37,99,235},5)
      .legend({"all flagged","chosen core: norm < 7"},{{220,38,38},{37,99,235}})
      .title("Same disk cloud: local cutoff changes the flags")
      .x_label("inclusive neighbour radius r").y_label("flagged sample count")
      .y_limits(0,p.size()*1.2).size(900,580).save_svg("build/cone_sensitivity.svg");
}
```
