\caption(The geometric cutoff changes direction work and classifications, while the complete ordered-pair count stays fixed. Small cutoffs can flag points deep in the chosen core; the narrow-angle control provides a separate sampling-sensitivity check.)
\alttext(Red total-flag and blue core-flag counts fall as the neighbourhood radius grows on the same fixed disk sample. The core count measures samples with radius below seven.)

> Work, duplicates and numerical contracts

The geometric rule is local, but the implementation scans every ordered i≠j
pair: exactly n(n−1) visits at every cutoff. It computes widened hypot distances
for noncoincident records and atan2 angles only for admitted neighbours. Sorting
k_i angles and checking their circular gaps gives

\[
O\!\left(n^2+\sum_i k_i\log k_i\right)\subseteq O(n^2\log n).
\]
\alttext(Work is the complete quadratic pair scan plus sorting each admitted neighbourhood, bounded by quadratic times logarithmic work overall.)

Analysis needs O(n) scratch/output storage. The optional trace additionally owns
all admitted directions, O(sum k_i), bounded by O(n²). The default complete pair
cap is ten million and is checked after full input validation, before allocation
or execution. The trace-only direction cap defaults to one million and applies
online to actual admitted directions. Zero means unlimited; analysis ignores the
direction cap, and the legacy mask-only call has no work cap. No failed check
returns a partial result. Counts exclude allocator costs, sort comparator counts
and elapsed time; sort_calls counts invocations, rather than sort comparisons.

Coincident records are not artificial zero-angle neighbours. The previous use
of atan2(0,0) could invent an eastward ray and fill a real gap. The checked core
excludes these records, reports them separately and keeps original identities
for all genuine directions. Every point and control is validated, including on
empty input: radius must be finite/positive and the full angular threshold must
be in (0,2π]. Widened differences/hypot avoid the former double squared-distance
overflow/underflow. On platforms without a wider working exponent range, extreme
differences can throw overflow_error. Angles and cutoff decisions remain rounded;
the implementation does not provide exact geometric predicates or hidden tolerances.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> triangle{{0,0},{1,0},{0,1}};
  dm::geometry::ConeSurfaceLimits limits;limits.max_pair_visits=6;limits.max_directions=6;
  const auto complete=dm::geometry::cone_surface_trace(triangle,2,3,limits);
  bool pair_limit=false,direction_limit=false,invalid=false;
  limits.max_pair_visits=5;
  try{(void)dm::geometry::cone_surface_analyze(triangle,2,3,limits);}catch(const std::length_error&){pair_limit=true;}
  limits.max_pair_visits=6;limits.max_directions=5;
  try{(void)dm::geometry::cone_surface_trace(triangle,2,3,limits);}catch(const std::length_error&){direction_limit=true;}
  try{(void)dm::geometry::cone_surface_analyze({},0,3);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}
  const auto gap=complete.analysis.points[0].largest_gap;
  const bool equal=dm::geometry::cone_surface_analyze(triangle,2,gap).points[0].surface;
  const bool above=dm::geometry::cone_surface_analyze(triangle,2,std::nextafter(gap,10.L)).points[0].surface;
  if(!pair_limit || !direction_limit || !invalid || !equal || above)return 1;
  const auto duplicate=dm::geometry::cone_surface_analyze({{0,0},{0,0},{0,1},{-1,0},{0,-1}},1,.75L*std::acos(-1.L));
  std::print("| actual contract check | result |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| triangle complete pair visits | {} |\n| triangle actual directions | {} |\n| threshold equals returned gap | {} |\n| one working ULP above gap | {} |\n| duplicate query directions | {} |\n| duplicate query coincident records | {} |\n| duplicate query flagged | {} |\n",complete.analysis.work.pair_visits,complete.analysis.work.angle_evaluations,equal,above,duplicate.points[0].neighbors,duplicate.points[0].coincident,duplicate.points[0].surface);
  std::print("\nPair cap five and actual-direction cap five reject their six-count workloads. Radius zero rejects even an empty input.\n");
  const double tiny=std::numeric_limits<double>::denorm_min();
  const auto small=dm::geometry::cone_surface_trace({{0,0},{tiny,0},{2*tiny,0},{0,tiny}},tiny,3);
  if(small.analysis.points[0].neighbors!=2)return 1;
  std::print("Subnormal cutoff admits {} genuine directions at the origin.\n",small.analysis.points[0].neighbors);
}
```
